# A village reads as hand-built, walked through on real input.
#
# The art review of wave A measured the spawn village on the canon seed: every
# house a rectangular prism, its outline long straight runs of near-black, its
# whole roof ONE ruled corrugation — the machines' idiom on a house people
# built. And seven houses drawn from four models, three of them the same.
#
# So this walks the square and looks at the houses from both sides, stands under
# one, crosses to a second village to prove the deal is not one seed's luck, and
# stays out to dark for the stolen neon the canon could not catch (art review 11:
# zero tube pixels in three frames, because the tube was on the door wall, which
# faces the square, and under the eave, which at this pitch hides it).
#   tools/tour.sh tours/houses.tour --seed=7 --weather=clear:0

coast calm
place spawn
hour 10.0
wait 0.6
shot 01-village-morning with prop:house

# Walk in among them: at play zoom, each house has to differ from its neighbour.
walk -1,-1 1.8
wait 0.4
shot 02-walked-in with prop:house

# Stand at a house and look at it from the ground: leaning walls, turf banked at
# the foot, salvage against it, a roof patched in several things.
near house
wait 0.6
shot 03-under-a-roof with prop:house
zoom 8
wait 0.4
shot 04-close-hand-built with prop:house
zoom 15

# The other side of the square: houses seen turned the other way, where the
# outline has to break just as much.
walk 1,0 2.2
wait 0.5
shot 05-from-the-other-side with prop:house

# Another village on the same seed: the deal is a rule, not one lucky village.
# On seed 7 this one (Coombe Wood, in the pinewood) wired nothing in, so it is
# also the proof that stolen neon is something a village did and not a filter
# over the coast — five houses, five silhouettes, no tube.
village 4
wait 0.8
shot 06-another-village with prop:house

# Dusk, then dark: the stolen tube runs the roof edge, so the camera has it
# whichever way the house was turned.
village 0
hour 20.2
wait 0.6
shot 07-village-dusk with prop:house
hour 22.5
wait 0.8
shot 08-village-night with prop:house
zoom 9
wait 0.5
# A `pixels:` floor is a COUNT of frame pixels, and the frame went from 1280x720
# to 3840x2160 — nine times the area — when LANTERN moved the base. The 60 here
# was written for the small frame and never rescaled, so the same tube now covers
# nine times the pixels and the floor asks for a ninth of what it meant. Measured
# on this very frame: 6232 pixels of tube against a floor of 60, which is a
# hundred times over. A frame holding one speck of the right hue passed as proof
# of stolen neon. 540 is the 60 the line meant, at this frame's size, and still
# leaves the tube an order of magnitude of room to be dimmed or moved.
# tours/canon.tour:120 (60), tours/landscape.tour:91 (40) and tours/works.tour:51
# (bebadf, 30) carry the same stale floors and have NOT been rescaled here,
# because nobody has measured what those three frames really hold and a floor
# raised without a measurement is the same mistake the other way round.
shot 09-stolen-neon-close with pixels:4df2ff+ff40cc+8cff59:540
zoom 15

# Wet: the tube mirrored in the ground is the frame the canon meant to protect.
weather rain:1
wait 1.4
shot 10-village-wet-night with prop:house
weather clear:0
